Title:
Sliver GUI — Desktop Operator Console for Sliver C2 (Wails v2)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- Sliver GUI is a native desktop operator console for the BishopFox Sliver C2 framework, aiming for a Cobalt Strike/Havoc-style workflow.  
- It acts as a thin Wails v2 (Go + HTML/CSS/JS) frontend over Sliver’s existing `rpcpb.SliverRPC` gRPC service, using the same mTLS operator `.cfg` files as `sliver-client` and reimplementing no C2 logic.  
- The tool focuses on operator usability: unified sessions/beacons management, per-agent and server consoles, interactive PTY shell over gRPC tunnels, and extension/BOF execution via Sliver’s normal RPC flows.  
- It adds visualization and orchestration features such as an interactive pivot/jump topology graph, scriptable “recipes” for post-exploitation actions (lateral movement, privesc, persistence, creds, enum), and operator panels for tracking IOCs and generating cleanup/report artifacts.  
- Useful primarily for Red Teams and pentesters running Sliver who want a richer operator UX without protocol drift or grpc-web proxies.  
- Interesting because it directly imports Sliver’s protobuf stubs in Go, reducing compatibility issues when upstream `.proto` changes and keeping parity with teamserver capabilities.

Technical Focus:
- Sliver `rpcpb.SliverRPC` gRPC integration (direct protobuf stubs)
- mTLS operator configuration (`.cfg`) and authenticated operator connectivity
- Operator console features: per-agent command execution, beacon tasking vs session interactivity
- Pivoting and topology visualization (pivot/jump graph, session-id chain joining)
- Implant generation workflows (mTLS/HTTP/DNS/WireGuard/tcp-pivot, profiles, builds)
- Extensions/BOFs and Armory management (list/install/remove)

Use Cases:
- Run Sliver operations via a desktop GUI instead of CLI (`sliver-client`)
- Visualize multi-hop pivot chains and lateral movement lineage during engagements
- Generate and manage implants and C2 profiles (including pivot transports like `tcp-pivot`)
- Execute post-exploitation playbooks (jump/spawn/remote exec) with dry-run and OpSec labeling
- Track engagement artifacts (loot/creds/hosts/events/IOCs) and produce cleanup/report outputs

Keywords:
Sliver, BishopFox, SliverRPC, gRPC, protobuf, mTLS, operator cfg, Wails v2, Go, PTY shell, beacon tasking, sessions, pivoting, SOCKS, port forwarding, WireGuard, DNS C2, HTTP C2, Armory, BOF, extensions, lateral movement, PsExec, WinRM, WMI, SSH, audit log, topology graph